{
 "idea": {
  "id": "overnight_persist",
  "family": "overnight",
  "title": "Stocks that have been rising overnight keep rising overnight",
  "why": "Some stocks are bought mostly by people who trade at the open (retail, overseas) and sold through the day by institutions, and that split persists for months: Lou, Polk and Skouras (2019) found a stock's overnight return over the past month predicts its overnight return next month, and the reverse for its intraday return. The trade is held close to open only, so it turns the whole book over every day; cost is the question.",
  "source": "Lou, Polk, Skouras 2019, A Tug of War",
